132
00:12:29,933 --> 00:12:31,714
[SPEAKER_01]: It's there due to stuff that you've done in the past.

133
00:12:31,734 --> 00:12:33,636
[SPEAKER_01]: But now, you are stuck with it.

134
00:12:34,456 --> 00:12:38,679
[SPEAKER_01]: So, then you just have to endure it and clearly see the distinction.

135
00:12:38,859 --> 00:12:45,643
[SPEAKER_01]: Wait, this is mind pressuring me and now it's up to me whether I act out of that pressure or not.

136
00:12:46,624 --> 00:12:50,626
[SPEAKER_01]: And in order to get that distinction clear, that is precisely the perspective.

137
00:12:51,707 --> 00:12:53,388
[SPEAKER_01]: The perspective upon your situation.

138
00:12:55,467 --> 00:12:59,530
[SPEAKER_01]: And so, if there's pressure, you cannot fundamentally not do things.

139
00:13:00,390 --> 00:13:12,258
[SPEAKER_01]: So, then, the wisdom is in learning, can I do things while that pressure is there, that are not, let's say, coming out of that pressure.

140
00:13:18,943 --> 00:13:21,385
[SPEAKER_02]: Another thing, recently, I found helpful with

141
00:13:30,439 --> 00:13:41,922
[SPEAKER_02]: When the mind is pressured, you know you should really restrain this tendency to act out.

142
00:13:43,702 --> 00:13:52,784
[SPEAKER_02]: Even if it's not breaking the precepts, or seems quite remote, beyond the scope of the precepts.

143
00:13:57,415 --> 00:14:01,476
[SPEAKER_02]: Not seeing any pressure as outside the scope of the precepts.

144
00:14:03,057 --> 00:14:08,278
[SPEAKER_02]: Makes sense.

145
00:14:08,518 --> 00:14:09,559
[SPEAKER_02]: That thread is the same.

146
00:14:12,019 --> 00:14:23,583
[SPEAKER_02]: And that if you feed, if you feed the mind now, then you keep going in that same direction, then eventually you would break the precepts.

147
00:14:25,984 --> 00:14:40,389
[SPEAKER_02]: Even if it's going for a walk, or muddling, or getting tangled up with doubt, it's still the same trajectory.

148
00:14:41,369 --> 00:14:42,609
[SPEAKER_02]: So, it's a kind of

149
00:14:47,058 --> 00:14:48,479
[SPEAKER_04]: Yeah, I don't know.

150
00:14:48,559 --> 00:14:59,443
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, I'm not sure if I follow, but if by keeping the precepts... Look, the whole point of keeping those precepts is for you to even begin to recognize what it means to be pressured by the mind.

151
00:14:59,483 --> 00:15:00,003
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah.

152
00:15:00,143 --> 00:15:00,383
[SPEAKER_01]: Right?

153
00:15:00,643 --> 00:15:04,905
[SPEAKER_01]: Because the starting point is you'll just be running with it, so you don't even see it.

154
00:15:05,749 --> 00:15:08,191
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, you have various good reasons for keeping the precepts.

155
00:15:08,831 --> 00:15:09,412
[SPEAKER_01]: You keep them.

156
00:15:09,792 --> 00:15:13,054
[SPEAKER_01]: And so, at some point, your mind wants to push you in that direction.

157
00:15:13,335 --> 00:15:16,757
[SPEAKER_01]: But now, you, being committed to those precepts, say, wait, I don't want to go there.

158
00:15:17,338 --> 00:15:22,621
[SPEAKER_01]: So, there's going to be somewhat of an internal, quote-unquote, conflict between your mind pushing you in one direction.

159
00:15:22,641 --> 00:15:26,985
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, at some point, you run against that fence, which is those precepts that you're keeping.

160
