173
00:16:23,012 --> 00:16:33,095
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, basically, that monk is declaring himself to the Buddha to be a noble disciple, because, you know, Sariputta, when he was asked in the Samādhiti Sutta, you know, how do you know what is the right view?

174
00:16:33,635 --> 00:16:42,357
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, the first thing Sariputta mentions is, well, here a noble disciple knows the wholesome and the root of the wholesome, and the unwholesome and the root of the unwholesome.

175
00:16:42,657 --> 00:16:44,138
[SPEAKER_01]: This is how someone is of the right view.

176
00:16:44,818 --> 00:17:02,861
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when the Buddha then asked that particular monk, do you see unwholesome as unwholesome, and if he then says fully, yes, I see all of that to the point that I can train in not doing anything unwholesome, he was basically already having the right view, so then he was on that middle way, he has understood that principle, okay, then just develop it.

177
00:17:05,463 --> 00:17:07,505
[SPEAKER_01]: But we should not be taking any liberties.

178
00:17:07,525 --> 00:17:10,106
[SPEAKER_04]: It's better to, eh... to be on the safe side.

